/T (Regulations such as India's DPDP Act and the GDPR expect personal data to be used only for specific, itemized purposes and corresponding processing to stop when consent is withdrawn. In practice, consent is logged but not enforced where data is actually shared, thus there is the requirement of a application which manages the a consent-management workflow, ensuring enhanced privacy and safety)
